[206.808951, "i", "cat > FIXES_APPLIED.md << 'EOF'\n# Checkpoint Resume Fixes\n\n## Bugs Fixed\n\n### Bug 1: Checkpoint saved batch number instead of line number\n**Problem:** The checkpoint saved `batch_num` (0, 1, 2...) but labeled it as 'last_line'. When resuming, it compared line numbers (0-50000) with batch numbers (0-50), causing it to skip only a few lines instead of thousands.\n\n**Fix:** Changed to track `lines_processed` and save the actual line number processed.\n\n### Bug 2: Database operations replaced instead of accumulated\n**Problem:** Used `INSERT OR REPLACE` which overwrites existing category data on resume, losing previously processed aggregations.\n\n**Fix:** Changed to `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` with accumulation:\n```sql\nINSERT INTO summary (category, total_value, count) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\nON CONFLICT(category) DO UPDATE SET\n    total_value = total_value + excluded.total_value,\n    count = count + excluded.count\n```\n\n### Bug 3: Checkpoint file not properly flushed\n**Problem:** Not using context manager and no expl"]
[206.809071, "i", "icit flush, so checkpoint might not be written to disk before a crash.\n\n**Fix:** Added proper context manager, explicit flush(), and fsync():\n```python\nwith open('.checkpoint', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump({'last_line': line_num}, f)\n    f.flush()\n    os.fsync(f.fileno())\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- Processed 20000 lines, then resumed and processed remaining 30000 lines\n- Final count: exactly 50000 records (no duplication or loss)\n- Re-running after completion remains idempotent\n- All categories properly aggregated\nEOF\n"]
